.TH SOC-OTA-PROVISION 1 "October 2026" "OTA-Pulse" "OTA-Pulse Manual"
.SH NAME
soc-ota-provision \- register a device with the OTA-Pulse backend
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soc-ota-provision
.BI \-\-server " URL"
.BI \-\-token " TOKEN"
[\fB\-\-device\-id\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Registers the device with a provisioning token, receives the per-device API key and stores it, together
with the device identity, in \fI/data/otapulse/otapulse.conf\fR (mode 0600). The running agent is restarted
to pick the credentials up. The credentials live on the data partition so that they survive A/B updates.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-server " URL"
Backend URL.
.TP
.BI \-\-token " TOKEN"
Provisioning token issued by the backend.
.TP
.BI \-\-device\-id " ID"
Device identifier. Defaults to the MAC address of the first Ethernet interface, then to the machine id.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Provision again even if the device is already provisioned.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR soc-ota-agent (1)
